<h1>Dev</h1><blockquote><p>Press <code>F5</code> to start debugging mode.</p></blockquote><p></p><h1>Deploy</h1><p>1. Build the bundle</p><pre><code>npm run build</code></pre><p>2. Package as a .vsix</p><pre><code>npx @vscode/vsce package --allow-missing-repository</code></pre><p>This produces hd-editor-0.1.0.vsix in the project root. You'll see warnings about missing repository, LICENSE, README.md etc. — those are fine to ignore for personal/internal use. If vsce refuses to package due to one of them, add --allow-missing-repository or create a stub file.</p><p></p><p>3. Install the .vsix into your main VS Code</p><p></p><pre><code>code --install-extension hd-editor-0.1.0.vsix --force</code></pre><p></p><p></p><p></p><pre><code>npm run build
npx @vscode/vsce package
code --install-extension hd-editor-0.1.0.vsix --force</code></pre><p></p>